# Circom Testing

Before changing a circuit or its wrapper, inspect the existing tests,
templates, inputs, outputs, component wiring, and TypeScript helpers. Test
through the public circuit or wrapper boundary rather than reproducing its
implementation in the test.

Cover, when applicable:

- valid witnesses and expected outputs;
- invalid witnesses rejected by constraints;
- zero, one, maximum, empty, duplicate, and malformed boundary cases;
- public/private signal visibility and signal ordering;
- field arithmetic and conversion boundaries;
- deterministic witness and proof inputs;
- serialization and deserialization round trips;
- proof verification and meaningful failure behavior.

Keep expected values independently derived. Do not use the same production
calculation as the test oracle, remove constraints to make a test pass, or
restrict valid inputs to hide a failure.

Use the repository workflow:

- `cd circuits && pnpm test`
- `cd circuits && pnpm build`
- `cd circuits && pnpm compile:ballot`
- `cd circuits && pnpm setup:ballot`

When compilation or setup changes generated artifacts, inspect exact output
ordering and retain only output attributable to the source change. Keep
external infrastructure setup outside arbitraries and clean up resources
created by tests.
